[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    134[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `randombytes.c` and `sphincs_core_det` from `rng.c`.  Both define
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `randombytes`, so only one can be linked at a time.  The `urandom` Cargo
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   feature selects the `/dev/urandom` version; the default matches the `driver`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   executable, which links `sphincs_core_det`.  Exported in all 96
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    138[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   configurations on both sides, with the provider switched by the feature.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **`randombytes_init`, `seedexpander{,_init}`, `AES256_ECB`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update`, `DRBG_ctx`** — these live only in `rng.c`, so the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `libsphincs_core.so` (urandom) does not have them.  The Rust `cdylib` keeps
